{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Close evidence: merged and independently re-verified\n\n- Gerrit change 1402, MERGED 2026-08-05 01:35:36 UTC with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n- Merged as commit c47cdcbfa8 on origin/main, carrying trailer rebar-ticket: 9a46-1c90-5dd9-44e1.\n\nIndependently re-verified against the MERGED tree, not just relayed from the fix agent:\n- AC2: src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py:30 now reads\n  class RunawayPaginationError(BackendPaginationStallError), so the subclass relation holds.\n- AC1/AC3/AC4: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_graph_pagination_heldout.py runs 49\n  passing tests against the merged tree, covering propagation through each of the three\n  enrichment sites plus negative controls proving ordinary non-stall failures still fail open.\n- AC3 specifically: the merged diff touches only acli_graph.py (+14/-1) and adds the new test\n  file. fetcher.py and all existing except-site tests are UNEDITED, which is what AC3 required.\n\nRoot cause for the record: the error subclassed RuntimeError, placing it outside\nBackendPaginationStallError's hierarchy, so the three re-raise clauses in fetch_snapshot never\nmatched a Cloud stall and the broad except Exception fail-open beneath each swallowed it into\na silently degraded snapshot."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785893810118090001,"uuid":"5e5d2799-6ab6-46a4-968a-e1155a7b7f45"}